{
  "category": "Uncategorized",
  "description": "Project Overview\nBuild a fully functional on-chain chess application on the Ethos blockchain with the following requirements:\n\nContext\n\nPlatform: Ethos blockchain\nAuthentication: Already implemented (Ethos login system is functional)\nUser Identity: Users are identified by their Ethos profile addresses\nTech Stack: [Specify: React/Next.js + Ethos docs(https://developers.ethos.network/api-documentation/api-v2)]\n\nCore Requirements\n1. Game Invitation System\nFeatures to Implement:\nA. Send Game Invitation\n\nCreate an \"Invite Player\" button prominently displayed on the main dashboard\nAllow users to invite opponents by entering their Ethos profile address\nImplement address validation to ensure the entered address is valid\nAdd optional game settings when sending invite:\n\nTime control (e.g., 10 min, 15 min, 30 min, unlimited)\nColor preference (White, Black, or Random)\nRated or Casual game\n\n\nDisplay confirmation message after successfully sending invitation\nShow error handling for invalid addresses or failed invitations\nPrevent users from inviting themselves\n\nUI Components:\n\n\"New Game\" button in navigation/header\nModal/popup with:\n\nInput field for opponent's Ethos address\nGame settings selector\n\"Send Invitation\" button\n\"Cancel\" button\n\n\n\nB. View Pending Invitations\n\nCreate an \"Invitations\" section/page accessible from main navigation\nDisplay two tabs:\n\nReceived Invites: Invitations sent to the current user\nSent Invites: Invitations the current user has sent to others\n\n\n\nReceived Invites Display:\n\nShow list of pending invitations with:\n\nOpponent's Ethos address (truncated with copy button)\nGame settings (time control, rated/casual)\nTimestamp of invitation\nTwo action buttons:\n\n\"Accept\" (green) - joins the game\n\"Decline\" (red) - rejects the invitation\n\n\n\n\nAdd notification badge showing count of pending invites\nDisplay \"No pending invitations\" message when empty\n\nSent Invites Display:\n\nShow list of outgoing invitations with:\n\nRecipient's Ethos address\nGame settings\nStatus (Pending, Accepted, Declined, Expired)\n\"Cancel Invitation\" option for pending invites\nTimestamp\n\n\n\nC. Join Game Flow\n\nWhen user accepts invitation:\n\nNavigate to game board immediately\nInitialize chess board with proper starting position\nDisplay opponent's address\nShow game settings (timer, etc.)\nStart the game automatically\n\n\nClear invitation from \"Received\" list after acceptance\nSend notification to inviter that game has started\n\n\n2. Chess Game Board Design\nVisual Design Requirements:\nA. Board Layout\n\n8x8 chess board with alternating light and dark squares\nStandard chess piece representation (Unicode symbols or SVG icons)\nClear distinction between:\n\nLight squares: #F0D9B5 or similar cream color\nDark squares: #B58863 or similar brown color\nLast move highlight: Semi-transparent yellow/green overlay\nSelected piece highlight: Border or glow effect\nValid moves indicator: Small dots or highlighted squares\nCheck indicator: Red highlight on king square\nCheckmate/Stalemate: Full board overlay with game result\n\n\n\nB. Game Information Panel\nDisplay alongside the board:\n\nPlayer Info:\n\nYour Ethos address (top)\nOpponent's Ethos address (bottom)\nCaptured pieces for each player\nMaterial advantage indicator\n\n\nGame Status:\n\nCurrent turn indicator (highlighted border around active player)\nTimer/clock for each player (if time control enabled)\nMove history/notation (scrollable list)\nMove counter\n\n\nGame Controls:\n\n\"Resign\" button\n\"Offer Draw\" button\n\"Request Rematch\" button (after game ends)\n\"Leave Game\" button\nMove navigation (for reviewing past moves)\n\n\n\nC. Move Notation\n\nDisplay algebraic notation for each move\nShow move pairs (White's move | Black's move)\nHighlight current position in move list\nAllow clicking moves to review position\nAuto-scroll to latest move\n\n. Chess Gameplay Functionality\nA. Core Game Mechanics\nMove Validation:\n\nImplement all legal chess moves for each piece:\n\nPawn: Forward movement, diagonal captures, en passant, promotion\nRook: Horizontal and vertical movement\nKnight: L-shaped movement\nBishop: Diagonal movement\nQueen: Combined rook and bishop movement\nKing: One square in any direction, castling\n\n\nPrevent illegal moves (moving into check, moving pinned pieces incorrectly)\nHighlight valid destination squares when piece is selected\nImplement drag-and-drop OR click-to-move functionality\n\nSpecial Moves:\n\nCastling:\n\nKingside (O-O)\nQueenside (O-O-O)\nValidate castling conditions (king/rook haven't moved, no pieces between, not in check, not castling through check)\n\n\nEn Passant:\n\nDetect when available\nHighlight as valid move\nExecute correctly\n\n\nPawn Promotion:\n\nShow promotion dialog when pawn reaches opposite end\nAllow selection of Queen, Rook, Bishop, or Knight\nDefault to Queen if no selection made\n\n\n\nGame State Detection:\n\nCheck: Highlight king in red, show \"Check!\" message\nCheckmate: Display winner, show game over modal\nStalemate: Display draw message, show game over modal\nInsufficient Material: Detect and declare draw\nThreefold Repetition: Track positions and declare draw\n50-Move Rule: Track and declare draw if applicable\n\nB. Turn Management\n\nLock board during opponent's turn\nOnly allow moving own pieces\nDisable interaction when game is over\nShow clear visual indicator of whose turn it is\nPrevent premature moves (if implementing time controls)\n\nC. Time Controls (if enabled)\n\nDisplay chess clocks for both players\nCount down only during active player's turn\nAdd time increment after move (if Fischer/Bronstein timing)\nFlag fall detection (time ran out = loss)\nPause timer during game review\n\n\n4. Game Lifecycle Management\nA. Active Games List\n\nCreate \"My Games\" section showing:\n\nActive Games:\n\nOpponent's address\nCurrent game state (Your turn / Opponent's turn)\nTime remaining (if applicable)\n\"Continue Game\" button\n\n\nCompleted Games:\n\nOpponent's address\nResult (Win/Loss/Draw)\nDate completed\n\"View Game\" button to review\n\n\n\n\n\nB. Game End Handling\n\nDisplay game over modal with:\n\nResult (Checkmate, Resignation, Draw, Timeout)\nWinner/Loser or Draw declaration\nFinal position\nMove count\nGame duration\n\"View Analysis\" button\n\"Rematch\" button\n\"New Game\" button\n\"Close\" button\n\n\n\nC. Game Actions\n\nResign:\n\nShow confirmation dialog\nUpdate game status immediately\nNotify opponent\n\n\nDraw Offer:\n\nSend offer to opponent\nOpponent sees \"Accept Draw\" / \"Decline Draw\" buttons\nCan be declined and game continues\n\n\nRematch:\n\nSend rematch invitation automatically to same opponent\nColors reversed from previous game\nSame settings as original game\n\n\n\n\n5. On-Chain Integration (Ethos/Move)\nSmart Contract Requirements:\nA. Game State Storage\n\nStore on-chain:\n\nGame ID (unique identifier)\nPlayer addresses (white, black)\nCurrent board position (FEN notation or custom encoding)\nMove history\nGame status (Active, Completed, Abandoned)\nGame result (if completed)\nTimestamps (created, last move, completed)\nGame settings (time control, rated/casual)\n\n\n\nB. Invitation System\n\nCreate invitation objects on-chain:\n\nInviter address\nInvitee address\nGame settings\nStatus (Pending, Accepted, Declined, Cancelled)\nExpiration time (auto-cancel after 24 hours)\n\n\n\nC. Move Validation\n\nValidate moves on-chain OR off-chain (specify approach)\nIf on-chain:\n\nImplement full chess rules in Move\nValidate each move before accepting transaction\n\n\nIf off-chain:\n\nValidate in frontend\nSubmit validated move to chain\nInclude move proof/signature\n\n\n\nD. Events/Notifications\n\nEmit events for:\n\nGame invitation sent\nInvitation accepted/declined\nMove made\nGame ended\nDraw offered/accepted\n\n\nUse events to trigger UI updates\n\n\n6. User Interface Navigation\nMain Navigation Structure:\n├── Dashboard (Home)\n│   ├── Quick Actions (New Game, View Invites)\n│   ├── Active Games List\n│   └── Recent Activity\n│\n├── Invitations\n│   ├── Received (with badge count)\n│   └── Sent\n│\n├── My Games\n│   ├── Active\n│   └── Completed\n│\n├── Profile\n│   ├── Ethos Address\n│   ├── Win/Loss/Draw Stats\n│   ├── Rating (if implementing ELO)\n│   └── Settings\n│\n└── [Active Game Board] (full screen when in game)\nResponsive Design:\n\nDesktop: Side-by-side board and game info\nTablet: Board above, info below\nMobile: Collapsible info panel, full-screen board\n\n\n7. User Experience Enhancements\nA. Notifications\n\nShow toast/snackbar notifications for:\n\nNew invitation received\nInvitation accepted\nYour turn (if user navigated away)\nGame ended\nDraw offered by opponent\n\n\n\nB. Real-time Updates\n\nPoll blockchain or use Ethos event subscriptions for:\n\nOpponent's moves\nNew invitations\nGame status changes\n\n\nUpdate UI automatically without page refresh\n\nC. Loading States\n\nShow loading indicators for:\n\nSending invitation\nAccepting invitation\nMaking moves\nLoading game state\nFetching invitations list\n\n\n\nD. Error Handling\n\nDisplay user-friendly errors for:\n\nInvalid Ethos address\nNetwork errors\nTransaction failures\nInvalid moves\n\n\nProvide retry options where appropriate\n\nE. Accessibility\n\nKeyboard navigation for chess board\nScreen reader support\nHigh contrast mode option\nMove announcement for visually impaired users\n\n\n8. Additional Features to Consider\nOptional Enhancements:\n\nChat System: Simple text chat between players during game\nGame Analysis: Post-game analysis showing blunders, best moves\nOpening Book: Show opening name if moves match known openings\nPuzzles: Daily chess puzzles for practice\nLeaderboard: Global or friends leaderboard\nAchievements: Badges for milestones\nExport Game: Download game in PGN format\nShare Game: Share game link or position\n\n\n9. Technical Implementation Notes\nState Management:\n\nUse React Context/Redux/Zustand for:\n\nCurrent game state\nUser authentication state\nActive invitations\nMove history\n\n\n\nChess Logic Library:\n\nConsider using chess.js or similar library for:\n\nMove validation\nGame state management\nFEN parsing\nCheck/checkmate detection\n\n\n\nBlockchain Interaction:\n\nUse Ethos SDK for:\n\nWallet connection (already done)\nTransaction signing\nSmart contract calls\nEvent listening\n\n\n\nData Structures:\ntypescriptinterface GameInvitation {\n  id: string;\n  inviter: string; // Ethos address\n  invitee: string; // Ethos address\n  timeControl: TimeControl;\n  rated: boolean;\n  status: 'pending' | 'accepted' | 'declined' | 'cancelled';\n  createdAt: number;\n  expiresAt: number;\n}\n\ninterface ChessGame {\n  id: string;\n  white: string; // Ethos address\n  black: string; // Ethos address\n  fen: string; // Current position\n  moves: string[]; // Move history in SAN\n  status: 'active' | 'checkmate' | 'stalemate' | 'draw' | 'resigned' | 'timeout';\n  winner?: string;\n  currentTurn: 'white' | 'black';\n  timeControl?: TimeControl;\n  whiteTime?: number;\n  blackTime?: number;\n  createdAt: number;\n  lastMoveAt: number;\n}\n\ninterface TimeControl {\n  initial: number; // seconds\n  increment: number; // seconds per move\n}\n\n10. Testing Checklist\nBefore deployment, ensure:\n\n Can send invitation to valid Ethos address\n Cannot send invitation to invalid address\n Cannot invite self\n Invitations appear in both sender and receiver's lists\n Can accept invitation and game starts\n Can decline invitation\n All piece movements work correctly\n Special moves (castling, en passant, promotion) work\n Check/checkmate/stalemate detection works\n Timer counts down correctly (if enabled)\n Can resign game\n Can offer and accept/decline draw\n Move history displays correctly\n Can view completed games\n Rematch functionality works\n Real-time updates work when opponent moves\n Error handling works for all edge cases\n\n\nDeliverables\n\nFunctional Chess Game Board with all standard chess rules implemented\nInvitation System with send/receive/accept/decline functionality\nGame Management interface showing active and completed games\nOn-chain Integration with Ethos blockchain for game state\nResponsive UI that works on desktop, tablet, and mobile\nReal-time Updates when opponent makes moves\nComprehensive Error Handling and loading states\n\n\nSuccess Criteria\n\nUsers can invite others using Ethos addresses\nUsers can view, accept, and decline invitations\nChess game follows all standard rules\nGames are stored on Ethos blockchain\nUI is intuitive and responsive\nReal-time updates work smoothly\nNo critical bugs in gameplay\n\n\nPlease implement this chess application following the specifications above, ensuring all core functionality is working before adding optional enhancements.\n\n",
